            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0510" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4331: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-20T13:00:00+08:00">February 20, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 20—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Japanese attack commenced 7:30 a.m., firing has been going on since 9
                    o’clock.</p>
                <p>My British colleague has made a last appeal to the Japanese to know if there is
                    any chance of good offices with a view of settlement. Japanese Minister informed
                    him matter now in hands of military and beyond his control, but that he was very
                    anxious to find some way out and thought perhaps after first fighting a chance
                    might offer. British colleague and myself are watching situation closely. We
                    will not leave until we feel sure no further efforts on our part possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
